<!--
  A cut-down NOAA ENC product catalogue, shaped like the real one.

  Structure copied from https://www.charts.noaa.gov/ENCs/12Region_ENCProdCat_19115.xml
  so that scripts/noaa-catalog.py can be tested without a download: coverage
  as an EX_BoundingPolygon of gml:pos values in LATITUDE-LONGITUDE order, the
  cell name as a citation title in a separate subtree, and the zip URL in a
  linkage.

  The cells and their approximate extents are real — US5CA72M is San Diego
  Bay at 1:12,000, US5CA71M its approaches, US5CA83M covers Santa Catalina,
  and US3CA14M is the Southern California overview that spans both. The
  geometry is simplified to four corners each; the catalogue's own polygons
  have more vertices, which this parser does not care about since it reduces
  them to a bounding box anyway.
-->
